# Copy this file to .env and fill in your Supabase project's values (Project Settings -> API).
# Both are safe to expose in the client bundle: EXPO_PUBLIC_* vars are inlined into the web/app
# build at build time, and the anon key is meant to be public -- real access control is done via
# Postgres Row Level Security policies (see supabase/schema.sql), not by keeping this key secret.
#
# If these are left unset, the app falls back to its original fully-local, in-memory/AsyncStorage
# mode (no shared backend, seed data only) -- this is what happens automatically inside the Claude
# Artifact preview, whose CSP blocks all outbound network calls anyway.

EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
